Exact one-duplicate strengthening:
  At length 70 and support size 69, count-use is a Boolean vector with
  total one. It identifies the unique duplicated edge.
  Multiplicity balance gives the exact support imbalance at every vertex.
  A nonloop duplicate forces local support degrees 1/2 at its prefix and
  2/1 at its suffix.
  A loop duplicate gives balanced support and therefore reduces to a
  distinct-window length-69 search when connectivity holds.
  The model also uses exact loop-dependent stationarity maxima and
  support-based autocorrelation cover rows.
  Optional pair-projection rows were implemented and tested but remain
  disabled by default after controlled wall-time runs were inconclusive.

