Solver-reported result:
  The ten partitioned anchors cover every connected distinct-window
  length-69 support.
  CP-SAT reported every overlap-at-least-58 anchor model INFEASIBLE.
  Under the tested exact formulation, a connected distinct-window 69-edge
  radius-1 covering cycle would need to replace at least 12 support edges.

Limitations:
  This is finite-neighborhood exact-model computational evidence around one
  support.
  It does not exclude repeated-window sequences or connected distinct-window
  supports with overlap 57 or below.
  It does not settle the existence of a 69-bit covering cycle.
  It does not establish a new upper or lower bound on L(9,1).
  CP-SAT did not emit an independently checkable proof trace. The repository
  therefore does not publish this as a formal infeasibility proof.
  The public mathematical interval remains 62 <= L(9,1) <= 71.
